solutions.latex:
At $x = 1$ read from the graph:

the curve is below the $x$-axis, so $f(1) < 0$;

the curve is decreasing, so $f'(1) < 0$;

the curve is concave up, so $f''(1) > 0$.

The gradient at $x = 1$ is a small negative number, closer to zero than $f(1)$ (about $-0.4$ against about $-1.1$), so $f(1) < f'(1) < 0 < f''(1)$.

